From 1da957764817c4554121a0f45e65f0decf7be23c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:43:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] linux: enable the 768 MHz disppll LUT entry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

cv181x_disppll set_rate is gated by g2_pll_rate_lut: a rate with no LUT
row returns -ENOENT and the pll silently keeps its previous setting. The
vendor table only enables 1188 MHz (postdiv=2); the ready-made 768 MHz
row (csr 0x00108101, ssc_set 419430400 — vendor values) is commented out.

Uncommenting it is the enabler for the board-dts reclock (assigned-clocks
in the arm64 board dts): disppll 768 MHz -> clk_cam0_200 = disppll/8 =
96 MHz, which makes 2 Mbaud exact on every dw-uart (96M/16/3, 0.00%
error) instead of the 1,562,500 ceiling the fixed 25 MHz uart clock
imposed. Applies to the whole sg200x family (SG2000 and SG2002 share the
cv181x clk driver).
---
 linux_5.10/drivers/clk/cvitek/clk-cv181x.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/linux_5.10/drivers/clk/cvitek/clk-cv181x.c b/linux_5.10/drivers/clk/cvitek/clk-cv181x.c
index 561fb1fcb..73b20aabd 100644
--- a/linux_5.10/drivers/clk/cvitek/clk-cv181x.c
+++ b/linux_5.10/drivers/clk/cvitek/clk-cv181x.c
@@ -1915,7 +1915,7 @@ static const struct {
 	// {.rate = 48000000, .csr = 0x00129201, .ssc_set = 629145600},
 	// {.rate = 406425600, .csr = 0x010E9201, .ssc_set = 594430839},
 	// {.rate = 417792000, .csr = 0x01109201, .ssc_set = 642509804},
-	// {.rate = 768000000, .csr = 0x00108101, .ssc_set = 419430400},
+	{.rate = 768000000, .csr = 0x00108101, .ssc_set = 419430400},
 	// {.rate = 832000000, .csr = 0x00108101, .ssc_set = 387166523},
 	// {.rate = 1032000000, .csr = 0x00148101, .ssc_set = 390167814},
 	// {.rate = 1050000000, .csr = 0x00168101, .ssc_set = 421827145},
